@startsalt
' Screen: Create Organization
' User Stories:
'   - As a new user, I want to create an organization to group my scripts and team members
'   - As a new user, I want the slug auto-derived from the org name with manual override
'   - As a new user, I want to see a helpful empty state with a clear next step after creation

{
  ' Top nav (minimal — pre-org context)
  {
    <b>codefre.sh</b>
    .
    keith@noizu.com | [Log Out]
  }
  ==
  ' Page header
  {
    <b>Create Your Organization</b>
    <i>Organizations group your scripts, team members, and API tokens.</i>
  }
  ==
  ' Form
  {+
    <b>Organization Name</b>
    "Acme Corp                          "
    <i>This is how your org appears throughout codefre.sh.</i>
    --
    <b>Slug</b>   <i>(auto-derived — you can edit)</i>
    "acme-corp                          "
    <color:red><b>! Slug "acme-corp" is already taken. Try "acme-corp-2" or choose another.</b></color>
    --
    "acme-engineering                   "
    <color:green>Slug "acme-engineering" is available.</color>
    --
    <i>Your org URL will be: https://app.codefre.sh/acme-engineering</i>
    ==
    [Create Organization]
    <i>By creating an org you agree to the Terms of Service.</i>
  }
  ==
  ' Post-creation empty state (conditional — shown after success)
  {+
    <color:green><b>Organization "Acme Engineering" created!</b></color>
    --
    <i>You're the Owner. Invite teammates in Settings > Members.</i>
    --
    <b>No scripts yet.</b>
    Get started by creating your first evaluation script.
    --
    [+ Create Your First Script]
    --
    or [Import from YAML] | [View API Docs]
  }
}

@endsalt
